// Gold leaf. The Stonemason sells it in OSRS for 130,000 and this shop now does too - the note at
// the top of poh_stone.inv said it belonged to whichever round wired the gilded furniture, and
// this is that round: the opulent rug and the gilded wall decoration are both made of it.
//
// 377's own gold leaf (obj 5580, ics_goldleaf) is a recoloured papyrus with no cost on it, left
// over from In Search of the Myreque. This is its own obj on the same model and recolour so that
// the quest's copy stays the quest's.
//
// cost is 100,000 because that is the item's VALUE in OSRS, and the Stonemason sells at 130% of
// value: 130,000, which is what he charges in the live game.
//
// It was 260,000 until 2026-09-15, fitted to make a wrong multiplier give the right answer -
// ^poh_stone_sell was 500, his BUYING ratio, and 260,000 x 0.5 is also 130,000. Gold leaf was the
// only one of his four that came out right that way, which is exactly why nothing noticed.
[gold_leaf]
name=Gold leaf
desc=Very delicate thin pressed gold.
model=obj_papyrus
recol1s=29494
recol1d=29539
2dzoom=940
2dyan=112
2dxan=248
cost=100000
members=yes
weight=20g

[cert_gold_leaf]
certlink=gold_leaf
certtemplate=template_for_cert

// Magic stone. Value 750,000, which is what the cost is; the Stonemason sells it for 975,000 and
// buys it back for 375,000, ten in stock.
//
// THE FIRST VERSION OF THIS OBJ SAID 4,000,000 AND THAT NUMBER WAS INVENTED. It went in with the
// costume room's cape rack on 2026-09-15, written from memory rather than read off the shop row,
// and then repeated in the commit message, the project doc and a battery check that compared it
// against itself. The wiki row is "10 | 1m | 975,000 | 375,000" and it took one fetch to get.
// Battery 48 now reads the sell column.
//
// The only thing in the build that asks for one is the level-99 magic cape rack, which is what it
// is for in OSRS as well. There is no rev-474 model for it in this cache, so it is the marble
// block's model recoloured - the same move the gold leaf makes on obj_papyrus, and honest about
// it here rather than silently.
[magic_stone]
name=Magic stone
desc=A magical stone, humming faintly.
model=obj_poh_marble_block
2dxan=220
2dyan=164
2dxof=-7
2dyof=-41
recol1s=11488
recol1d=6684
cost=750000
members=yes
weight=13607g

[cert_magic_stone]
certlink=magic_stone
certtemplate=template_for_cert

// The seven bagged hedges the formal garden's Hedging hotspot is built from - one bag per
// hedge, which is the whole cost in OSRS as well. The Garden Centre sells them at their value
// (5,000 to 100,000) and buys back at 40%, the same as the ten bagged plants it already stocks.
//
// They are the SAME MODEL as everything else in a sack: OSRS ships all of them on obj 12307 and
// tells them apart by name, which is why the ten trees collapsed onto obj_poh_bagged and these
// seven do too. Nothing new was imported for this - the art that was missing was never the bag.

[poh_bag_thorny_hedge]
